00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.509 align:start position:0%
 
good morning  so concerning the covet 19 vaccines we  have reached an important milestone  the european union has exported so far  over 1 billion of covet 19 vaccines to  the rest of the world  vaccines from the european union have  been shipped to more than 150 countries  just to name a few to japan to turkey to  the uk to new zealand to south africa to  brazil  and important is  we delivered  around 87 million doses to the low and  middle-income countries  through covax  so we made good on our promise  we have always shared our vaccination  production and capacity fairly with the  rest of the world we've said that at  least every second doses produced in the  european union will go abroad and we  have reached that with this important  milestone of exporting 1 billion doses  of vaccines to the world  while also delivering in parallel to the  european citizens  the european union has achieved within  the european union now the goal to have  more than 75  of the adult population fully vaccinated  but remained we remained open during all  this time  we continued to export even when the  vaccines were scarce here in the  european union because we know and we  knew that we will only beat covet 19 the  pandemic if we vaccinate the whole world  therefore together with president biden  we aim for a global vaccination rate of  70  by next year  the eu us agenda for beating the global  pandemic will help to achieve that  the european union is doing expert on  top of our experts  we will donate  at least 500 million doses of vaccines  to the most vulnerable countries  but we know that other countries also  have to step up so i will work closely  with prime minister draghi and president  biden to rally g20 leaders next week at  the summit in rome  behind this very ambitious goal that's  the only way to beat the pandemic thank  you

